PROVENANCE
================================================================================

Ancoda Atlas began as a derivative of an existing open-source project licensed
under the GNU Affero General Public License v3.0, and has since been
substantially rewritten and re-scoped by Ancoda Labs to cover natural hazards in
Nepal only.

Because the AGPL-3.0 is a copyleft licence, this project and every derivative of
it must also be distributed under the AGPL-3.0. See CONTRIBUTING.md for what
that means for contributors, and README.md for what it means for anyone
deploying Atlas as a network service.


================================================================================
THIRD-PARTY DATA AND CONTENT
================================================================================

Administrative boundary data
    frontend/public/data/flood-affected-districts.json
    frontend/public/data/nepal-districts.geojson
    frontend/public/data/nepal-provinces.geojson
    backend/content/geo/flood-affected-districts.json

    The backend copy is the same file. It is read server-side to resolve a
    river gauge's district from its coordinates; the frontend copies are served
    to the browser for the maps.

    Derived from openknowledgenp/localboundaries
    https://github.com/openknowledgenp/localboundaries
    Licensed under the MIT License.

    The flood subset has been reduced to the affected districts and lowered in
    coordinate precision. nepal-provinces.geojson and nepal-districts.geojson
    are further simplified (mapshaper, keep-shapes) so a 3G phone is not asked
    to download the full vertex set. The MIT licence text is reproduced below.


Relief-fund and helpline content
    content/bhotekoshi-flood/

    Compiled by Ancoda Labs from primary sources, each recorded in the record's
    own "source" or "source_verification_url" field. Bank account details and
    QR codes originate from the Government of Nepal appeal published by the
    Office of the Prime Minister and Council of Ministers.

    Payment QR images under public/qr/ are Government of Nepal artefacts
    reproduced for public benefit. They are not Ancoda Labs property.


Live data services
    Atlas queries the following services at runtime. It does not redistribute
    their data in bulk, and each remains subject to its own terms of use.

    United States Geological Survey (USGS)      earthquake catalogue
    Open-Meteo                                  weather and air quality
    NASA FIRMS                                  satellite fire detection
    ReliefWeb (UN OCHA)                         humanitarian reporting
    Humanitarian Data Exchange (HDX)            ReliefWeb fallback datasets
    BIPAD Portal (NDRRMA, Government of Nepal)  river gauge telemetry
    Nepali news publishers                      hazard reporting via public RSS


